  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying a sure (certain) outcome in either lottery and preferring the one that has it. However, neither lottery contains a sure outcome, so the reason cannot be applied meaningfully. Furthermore, the individual did not refer to certainty or sure outcomes in their reasoning. Instead, they focused on the relative likelihood of getting zero, which is a different decision principle (e.g., minimizing the chance of the worst outcome). There is no alignment between the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) and what the individual considered (probabilities of non-zero outcomes). Also, the justification provided does not match the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
